WEBVTT

00:18:28.895 --> 00:18:31.773
and if you use that consistently
in your decision-making,

00:18:31.773 --> 00:18:33.859
it should not be a trade-off.

00:18:33.900 --> 00:18:36.111
These are not mutually exclusive things.

00:18:36.153 --> 00:18:38.697
SM: Anjali, how have you been
taking care of yourself

00:18:38.697 --> 00:18:42.659
during this period
of tremendous turmoil and change,

00:18:42.701 --> 00:18:44.161
but also growth?

00:18:44.202 --> 00:18:46.997
You mentioned you just had a baby.

00:18:47.038 --> 00:18:48.582
There's a lot on your shoulders.

00:18:48.582 --> 00:18:51.751
How, as a leader,
do you practice some self-care

00:18:51.751 --> 00:18:55.589
or how do you make sure
that you're getting the balance you need

00:18:55.630 --> 00:18:57.841
to be the most effective
leader you can be?

00:18:57.883 --> 00:18:59.050
AS: I think --